INE HOT-FIX, outside normal queue cadence", :intent "declare-urgent-intervention", :target "stop-the-line hot-fix", :rationale "The line is explicitly stopped and a hot-fix is declared as an exception to the normal queue cadence, which frames the rest of the status line."}, :roles ["contrast" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk", :objects {:G {:text "    This preserves speed on low-stakes actions while protecting high-stakes decisions.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'STOP-THE-LINE HOT-FIX, outside normal queue cadence'; pattern THEN: escalate when risk cost exceeds a threshold and log the comparison basis.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Escalate out of cadence explicitly and visibly: stop the line, label the action a hot-fix so the exception is on the record."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 84-105 'STOP-THE-LINE HOT-FIX' declares the intervention; pattern IF: a decision could carry material risk or irreversible impact.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A defect in an evidence-store sibling may carry material risk to the boot-reachable chain, warranting an interruptive decision."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination costs discourage escalation, while risk-blind escalation wastes time on low-stakes work.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Fragment 107-135 'outside normal queue cadence'; pattern HOWEVER: coordination costs discourage escalation while risk-blind escalation wastes time.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Normal queue cadence would defer the fix (coordination discipline), but waiting risks letting a high-stakes defect ride the queue."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Estimate risk cost (impact x likelihood) and compare it to coordination cost. Escalate when risk cost exceeds a defined threshold, and log the comparison basis.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/escalation-cost-vs-risk.flexiarg", :sha256 "90aecb75956504570d44d401650655b8bc660e3d023cd2e6aead3c5f08301fab"}, :situation-source "Pattern BECAUSE: preserves speed on low-stakes actions while protecting high-stakes decisions; the fragment names both the stop and the cadence exception.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Marking the exception preserves queue speed for ordinary work while protecting the high-stakes fix from cadence delay."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost", :source-sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a", :pattern-rationale "Delegating via a tracked issue is chosen over leaving work idle, acknowledging coordination cost as a real spend.", :fragment-index 2, :sentence-id "s1", :fragment {:start 139, :end 200, :text "Three remaining siblings handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65", :intent "delegate-remaining-work", :target "three remaining siblings", :rationale "The unfinished siblings are delegated to another agent through a tracked external issue, creating a dependency on that handoff."}, :roles ["action" "dependency"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/coordination-has-cost", :objects {:G {:text "    Cost-aware coordination prevents both under-use (never asking for help when stuck) and over-use (constant interruption). It respects the resources of collaborators.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment text 'handed to Codex via GitHub issue #65'; pattern THEN: include coordination cost in decision-making unless risk of error is higher than the cost.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Spend the coordination cost deliberately once, on a tracked issue, rather than piecemeal or not at all — the risk of the siblings stalling exceeds the handoff cost."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent wants to leverage external capabilities or get authoritative answers.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Fragment 139-200: work 'handed to Codex'; pattern IF: the agent wants to leverage external capabilities.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Finishing the three siblings needs work the author is not doing itself, so external capability (Codex) is being leveraged."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Coordination is not free: it takes time, consumes attention, introduces latency, and may require context transfer. Treating it as free leads to over-reliance or spamming.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/coordination-has-cost.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4cb887acc90b53511b2a56a502b1a2a188d862a0fbbd7e666e746e34644171a"}, :situation-source "Pattern HOWEVER: coordination takes time, attention, and context transfer; the fragment shows the cost being paid via a written GitHub issue.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Delegating costs something: authoring the issue, transferring context, and accepting latency on the siblings' completion."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Model coordination as an action with explicit cost (latency, tokens, human attention units). Include this cost in decision-making: sometimes working with partial local knowledge is better than waiting for external input, unless the risk of error is higher than the coordin